but having the best buys isn't the only thing

10
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:28,190
让一家"最值买"荣登最值的"最值买"
that makes a Best Buy the best Best Buy.

11
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:33,340
那最值"最值买"怎么样才能担起这头衔呢
What makes a best Best Buy the best Best Buy?

12
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:35,110
这问题问得好
Mm, that's a great question.

13
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:37,720
我喜欢它们开在墨西哥快餐店旁
I like when they're next to a Chipotle.

14
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,870
好了  我该去把行李拿出来了
Okay, well, I should unpack.

15
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:41,690
好的
All right.

16
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:43,820
好好享受神经生物学大会吧
Enjoy the neurobiology conference.

17
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:44,880
我会的
I will.

18
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:47,690
我...  真希望你也在这里
I... wish you were here.

19
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:49,650
参加神经生物学大会吗
At a neurobiology conference?

20
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:51,910
这话也太损了吧
What a mean thing to say.

21
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:56,670
好吧  那我很庆幸你不在这里呢
Okay, I'm glad you're not here?

22
00:00:56,670 --> 00:00:58,500
真好  每次只要我一教
Aw, you always know just what to say

23
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,770
你就会把话说到我心坎里
after I tell you what to say.

24
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:02,900
再见啦  谢尔顿
Good-bye, Sheldon.

25
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,070
再见
Bye.

26
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:06,320
好消息  各位
Oh! Good news, gentlemen.

27
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,180
艾米这周末去参加会议
Amy's at a conference this weekend,

28
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:11,310
这就代表你们有荣幸能娱乐本皇
which means I'm available to be entertained, hmm.

29
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:13,010
也就是现在年轻人说的
As today's youth might put it:

30
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:15,670
谁有兴趣来"谢"主隆恩啊
Who wants to get their Sheld-on?

31
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,360
我跟妮妮要为家里的重新装修做准备
Bernie and I are getting the house ready for the remodel.

32
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:21,090
我们很乐意有你来帮忙
We could always use an extra pair of hands.

33
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:23,200
一听就烂透了  拉杰呢
That sounds awful. Raj?

34
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:26,580
这周末我已预定好使用太空望远镜控制室
Uh, I've got time booked in the telescope room all weekend

35
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:27,980
来搜索流浪行星
scanning for rogue planets.

36
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:29,160
欢迎你跟我一起去
You're more than welcome to join me.

37
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:31,030
列入考虑  莱纳德呢
That's the one to beat. Leonard?

38
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:34,640
你别来烦我就"谢"天谢地了
Oh, if anything, I'm trying to get my Sheld-off.

39
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:37,560
看来冠军得主已经出炉  恭喜你
Well, then it looks like we have a winner. Congratulations.

40
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:40,400
先提醒你  那只是单纯坐在电脑前
Well, I should warn you, it's just looking at data

41
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,310
看好几小时的数据而已
for hours and hours on a computer screen.

42
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:45,130
已经选你  别再诱惑我了
Uh, stop selling it, kid. You won.

43
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
第九季  第十二集

44
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
炸

45
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
爆

46
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
大

47
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
活

48
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,360
生

49
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:14,580
今天好吗
How was your day?

50
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,670
不太好
Oh, not good.

51
00:02:15,670 --> 00:02:17,640
还是没能见到加洛医生
Still couldn't get in to see Dr. Gallo.

52
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,120
医生吗
A doctor?

53
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,700
你的病可别有传染性啊
Well, I hope you're not contagious.

54
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,270
我这周末要去太空望远镜控制室
I've got a weekend in the telescope room

55
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:26,990
我可是为此兴奋了将近有三分钟呢
I've been excited about for almost three minutes.

56
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,900
我没生病  是工作啦
I'm not sick. It's for work.

57
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,590
有一个医生拒绝见任何医药销售员
There's this doctor who refuses to see any sales reps.

58
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:33,990
我试着要见这医生好几个月了
I've been trying to get in for months.

59
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:35,250
你有穿那件
Well, did you try wearing the shirt

60
00:02:35,250 --> 00:02:37,110
我说上班穿太骚的衣服试试吗
I said was inappropriate for work?

61
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:39,540
那是个女医生  不过...
Well, the doctor's a woman, but...

62
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:42,080
穿了  毕竟"直弯"试过才知道
yes, because you never know.

63
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,440
她是什么医生
What kind of doctor is she?

64
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,180
精神科医生  怎么了
Um, a psychiatrist. Why?

65
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:48,810
那你假装自己是病人去预约呢
Well, what if you make an appointment as a patient?

66
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:50,150
那你就有机会跟她谈啦
Then you'll get to talk to her.

67
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:52,580
他们已经知道我是医药销售员了
Yeah, they already know I'm a pharmaceutical sales rep.

68
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,730
那如果是莱纳德假装病人去预约
Oh. What if Leonard made an appointment

69
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:56,690
先帮你铺好路呢
and tried to lay some groundwork for you?

70
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:58,250
这个主意有意思
That's interesting.

71
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,960
我才不要假装病人去看精神科医生
I'm not gonna make a fake appointment with a psychiatrist.

72
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,320
我要假装有啥毛病呢
What would I say is wrong with me?

73
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,730
-自尊低落  -社交焦虑
- Low self-esteem. - Social anxiety.

74
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:05,350
性生活不安全感
Sexual insecurity.

75
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,680
你们说得都不是真的
None of that is true.

76
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:11,490
否认现实  亲爱的  毛病多得很啊
Uh, denial. See, sweetie, the list goes on and on.

77
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:13,290
这也太扯了吧
That's just crazy.

78
00:03:13,290 --> 00:03:14,910
我去了对你有什么帮助啊
How would my going in there even help you?

79
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:17,390
不知道啊  你可以跟她聊天  谈到药时
I don't know. You could talk to her, and maybe if it comes up,

80
00:03:17,390 --> 00:03:18,930
就顺势问问她有没听过我公司的药
you could ask if she's heard about the drug.

81
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:20,090
万一被抓到怎么办
What if I get caught?

82
00:03:20,090 --> 00:03:21,390
-害怕失败  -缺乏自信
- Fear of failure! - Lack of confidence!

83
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:23,060
有点怂逼
Kind of a wuss!

84
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:26,400
行  我去
Fine, I'll do it.

85
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,530
但不是因为他们的话  是因为我爱你
But not because of them, because I love you.

86
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:29,310
谢谢
Thank you.

87
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,470
-软柿子   -没骨气
- Pushover. - Spineless.

88
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:34,380
两天前就交代去买牛奶  到现在都还没买
Still hasn't bought milk even though I told him two days ago!

89
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:39,550
真是爽翻天了
That was incredible.

90
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:42,240
的确
It was.

91
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,910
要是斯图尔特不在就更好了
I just wish Stuart wasn't around

92
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:46,190
我们想多大声就能多大声
so we didn't have to be so quiet.

93
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:47,210
对啊
I know.

94
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:48,970
而且这家伙看日本色情动画时
It's not like he returns the favor

95
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:53,190
也不知放大声点回报咱们
when he watches his Japanese porn cartoons.

96
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,680
你们俩有空吗
You guys got a minute,

97
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,630
还是还在事后抱抱
or are you still cuddling?

98
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,620
有事吗  斯图尔特
What is it, Stuart?

99
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:01,960
我能进来吗
Can I come in?

100
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,550
稍等
Hang on.

101
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,280
要不要我赶他走
Should I send him away?

102
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,560
不用  没事
No, it's okay.

103
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,000
谢谢你  妮妮
Thanks, Bernie.

104
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,760
你要干嘛
What's up?

105
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:15,680
我知道你们很快要重新装修了
Uh, well, I know the remodel is coming up,

106
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,630
所以我想让你们方便作业
so I thought I'd make it easy on you guys

107
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:19,780
就出去找房子
and find my own place.

108
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:23,640
我真没想到今晚能"好事"成双啊
I thought I was done getting lucky tonight.

109
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,260
所以你计划什么时候搬
So, when are you thinking of moving?

110
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:28,260
其实我已经找好一间公寓了
Uh, actually, I already found an apartment,

111
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,040
所以过几天就搬
so in a couple of days.

112
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:32,350
好吧
Oh. Okay.

113
00:04:33,090 --> 00:04:35,540
真舍不得你走咩
Sorry to see you go?

114
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:39,440
谢谢你们这些日子来的照顾
Okay, well, thank you guys for everything.

115
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,160
我真的非常感谢
I-I really appreciate it.

116
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,780
不用客气
You're very welcome.

117
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:48,030
怎么了
What?

118
00:04:48,030 --> 00:04:52,610
我只是从来没在你们醒着的时候进来过
Hmm, I just have never been in this room while you're awake.

119
00:05:02,910 --> 00:05:04,280
你在干嘛
What are you doing?

120
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:08,450
确保望远镜的摄像机白场已平衡
Uh, making sure the telescope's camera is white-field balanced.

121
00:05:10,090 --> 00:05:11,650
那现在呢
What are you doing now?

122
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:14,480
还在确保望远镜的摄像机
Still making sure the telescope's camera

123
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,620
白场已平衡
is white-field balanced.

124
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:16,970
了解
Oh, I see.

125
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,840
那现在呢
How about now?

126
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:27,650
现在在确保望远镜的摄像机白场已平衡
Now I'm making sure the telescope's camera is white-field balanced

127
00:05:27,650 --> 00:05:29,450
以及后悔你没有一本彩色填色本
and wishing you had a coloring book.

128
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,670
我可以帮上忙啊
Well, I can be helpful.

129
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:33,020
给我点事情做做嘛
Give me something to do.

130
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,820
告诉你  有一次我爹带我去上班
You know, my father took me to work once,

131
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:36,280
才十分钟我就发现了
and in ten minutes I figured out

132
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,110
到底是谁从收银机里偷钱
who'd been stealing from the cash register.

133
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,930
就是我爹
It was my father.

134
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,260
我爹丢了工作
Yeah, Dad lost his job,

135
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:45,450
但是他老板给了我根软糖冰棒
but Mr. Hinckley gave me a Fudgsicle.

136
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,980
行  你想要来点事做是吧
Fine, you want something to do?

137
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,810
这硬盘里有搜集了大约六个月的数据
There's about six months of data on this hard drive.

138
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:52,690
你何不过一遍这些数据  看能否发现
Why don't you go through it and see if you can spot

139
00:05:52,690 --> 00:05:54,350
有任何规律或异常呢
any patterns or anomalies.

140
00:05:54,350 --> 00:05:55,540
好的  我这就去
Yep, I'm on it.

141
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:56,530
你看我们
Hey, look at that!

142
00:05:56,530 --> 00:06:00,430
印度阿三把电脑工作外包给白人佬
An Indian guy outsourcing a computer job to a white fella.

143
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,620
随便怎么样
Yeah, okay, whatever it takes

144
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:05,740
只要能让你忙个数小时就行了
to keep you busy for a few hours.

145
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,140
找到一个
Found one.

146
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,310
不可能
No, you didn't.

147
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:11,680
那有好几百万数据点呢
There are millions of data points there.

148
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,460
可是你看  一个光学瞬态
But, look, an optical transient.

149
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,340
好吧  可能真的有东西
Yeah, maybe that is something.

150
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:18,430
-你怎么发现的  -其实不难啦
- How did you find that? - It wasn't difficult.

151
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:21,510
就像质数在你眼里自动就是红色的
You know how when you see prime numbers, they appear red,

152
00:06:21,510 --> 00:06:22,900
孪生质数是粉红色
but when they're twin primes,

153
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,730
而且闻起来像汽油  你懂我的意思吗
they're pink and smell like gasoline?

154
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:27,930
不懂
No.

155
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:31,910
可能我与众不同吧
I guess I'm a special boy.

156
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,900
有时候当一个男孩与众不同
You know, sometimes when a boy is special,

157
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,870
他会得到一根软糖冰棒
he gets a Fudgsicle.

158
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:39,480
而且味道尝起来像光速
Which, by the way, tastes like the speed of light.

159
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,470
非常感谢你能临时抽空见我
Thank you for seeing me on such short notice.

160
00:06:44,470 --> 00:06:45,830
乐意效劳
Ah, it's my pleasure.

161
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:47,300
我很好奇
I'm curious,

162
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,600
你和贝弗莉·霍斯塔特博士是亲戚吗
are you related to Dr. Beverly Hofstadter?

163
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:52,100
她是我母亲  你认识她吗
Uh, she's my mother. You know her?

164
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,390
不  不认识本人
No, not personally,

165
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:55,500
但我读过她所有的书
but I have read all of her books.

166
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,840
那你对她的认识比我还深
Well, then you know her better than I do.

167
00:06:58,430 --> 00:06:59,740
不见得
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

168
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:01,570
但我可以告诉你
But I can tell you I do not agree

169
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:04,720
我完全不同意她育儿的那套理论
with her theories on child rearing at all.

170
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:05,970
是咩
Really?

171
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:09,440
你是不是觉得那一套过于冷漠残酷
Any chance you find them cold, cruel and unsuitable

172
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:12,180
并不适合天真无邪  想快乐生活的小男生
for innocent little boys who just want to be happy?

173
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,260
我不想妄加评论
Well, I didn't want to say it...

174
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:16,050
不不  请评论  唱出来
No, no, say it. Sing it.

175
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:18,510
租一架飞机  写在天空
Rent a plane, write it in the sky.

176
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:20,630
听起来你对她
Sounds like you're holding on

177
00:07:20,630 --> 00:07:22,520
一直心怀怨念  怒气满满啊
to quite a bit of anger towards her.

178
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:24,440
不  我已经努力克服不少怨念
Oh, no, I-I've worked through a lot of that stuff;

179
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,220
-现在好多了  -那就好
- I'm better now. - Good for you.

180
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:28,420
你知道她从不让我庆祝自己的生日
Do you know she never let me celebrate my birthday

181
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:31,550
就因为我的出生是她的成就  不是我自己的吗
